<article class="env-lemma" id="0692">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0692">Lemma <span data-tag="0692">31.22.11</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to X$ be a Koszul regular closed immersion. Then there exists a surjective smooth morphism $X' \to X$ such that the base change $i' : Z \times _ X X' \to X'$ of $i$ is a regular immersion. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We may assume that $X$ is affine and the ideal of $Z$ generated by a Koszul-regular sequence by replacing $X$ by the members of a suitable affine open covering (affine opens as in Lemma <a href="/tag/063G" data-tag="063G">31.21.7</a>). The affine case is More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/068Q" data-tag="068Q">15.31.17</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>